It is Saturday morning.
I am walking with Moti in the local park.
The weather is very pleasant today.
Moti is walking happily ahead of me.
He stops suddenly near a big tree.
He looks up and wags his tail.
A small squirrel is running on the branch.
Moti barks loudly and pulls the leash.
He wants to chase the squirrel.
I hold the leash tight.
"Moti, no!"
"Stop!" I tell him.
"Come here!"
"Sit down!"
I remember Asha's strict rule.
He must be kept on the leash in the park.
I must not let him loose here.
The squirrel climbs higher up the tree.
"Good boy," I say and pat his head.
Moti finally sits quietly next to me.
We start our walk again.
